  "abstract_summary": "Static program analysis finds bugs before software ships, and modern checkers for C/C++ depend on whole-program infrastructure: pointer analysis, value-flow tracking, taint analysis, and IFDS-based data flow on top of LLVM. Today\u2019s LLVM-IR frameworks fall short. SVF, Phasar, and Lotus expose their analyses through C...",
